Article 3 (Fisheries Day)
(1) To commemorate Fisheries Day under Article 5 of the Framework Act on Fisheries and Fishing Villages Development (hereinafter referred to as the "Act"), the State and local governments may hold the following events:
1. Commemorative events for Fisheries Day;
2. Research presentations and international exchange events for the promotion of fisheries and fishing villages;
3. Encouragement and awards for persons or organizations that have contributed to the promotion of fisheries and fishing villages;
4. Publicity events through mass media, etc. concerning fisheries and fishing villages;
5. Other events to enhance nationwide interest in fisheries and fishing villages.
(2) In principle, the commemorative event under paragraph (1) 1 shall be held on April 1 of each year: Provided, That where April 1 falls on a Saturday or public holiday, the timing of the event may be adjusted.
